message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Most big US local-government PDFs fail basic accessibility checks"
abstract: "Of 5,412 PDFs read from the websites of large US cities and counties, 22.0% pass four basic machine checks that screen readers rely on. Files made since the 2024 ADA Title II rule do better, and the software that made a file decides most of the outcome. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
